WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Vietnamese narration script. Timing is distributed proportionally within each slide segment, since the narration itself is in Vietnamese.

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.847
Hello everyone, this is the revision video for Chapter Five:

2
00:00:03.847 --> 00:00:05.517
Drafting and presenting documents.

3
00:00:05.517 --> 00:00:09.600
This is the chapter that turns every spoken agreement into a legally valid document.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.025
Under Decree 30/2020/ND-CP of the Government on clerical work:

5
00:00:15.025 --> 00:00:18.245
a document is written information conveyed in language or symbols,

6
00:00:18.245 --> 00:00:21.515
produced in the course of an agency's or organisation's activities,

7
00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:24.393
and presented in the proper form and technique as required.

8
00:00:24.393 --> 00:00:27.405
There are four groups of documents: legal normative documents,

9
00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:31.000
administrative documents, specialised documents, and commercial documents.

10
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.746
As for content, a document must meet four requirements:

11
00:00:35.746 --> 00:00:38.434
serve the right purpose and stay within the issuer's authority;

12
00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:41.334
be accurate and objective; be clear, concise and easy to understand;

13
00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:44.022
and comply with the law and use proper administrative language,

14
00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:45.600
with absolutely no colloquial speech.

15
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.752
Here is the diagram you should save: the nine formality components on an A4 page.

16
00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:56.096
The national title and motto sit in the top right corner.

17
00:00:56.096 --> 00:01:00.731
The issuing body's name is in the top left, with the reference number below it.

18
00:01:00.731 --> 00:01:03.547
The place and date of issue sit below the motto.

19
00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:06.891
The document type and its summary line sit in the middle.

20
00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:08.240
Then comes the content.

21
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.153
The signatory's title, name and signature sit in the bottom right,

22
00:01:12.153 --> 00:01:13.872
along with the agency's seal.

23
00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:16.453
The distribution list is in the bottom left.

24
00:01:16.453 --> 00:01:17.459
One special note:

25
00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:23.200
an official letter has no type heading — its summary line starts with “V/v”, meaning “regarding”.

26
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.037
The figures on formatting technique you must know by heart: A4 paper;

27
00:01:30.037 --> 00:01:33.702
top and bottom margins twenty to twenty-five millimetres;

28
00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:38.075
left margin thirty to thirty-five millimetres, to allow for binding;

29
00:01:38.075 --> 00:01:40.840
right margin fifteen to twenty millimetres.

30
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.475
Times New Roman font, Unicode encoding, size thirteen to fourteen, black.

31
00:01:45.475 --> 00:01:49.330
Page numbers start from the second page, in Arabic numerals,

32
00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.000
centred at the top margin.

33
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.928
For administrative documents, remember what's distinctive about each type:

34
00:01:56.928 --> 00:01:58.979
a decision is written in numbered Articles,

35
00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:01.363
with the final Article stating its effective date.

36
00:02:01.363 --> 00:02:04.708
A proposal memo has three parts: reason, proposed plan, recommendation.

37
00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:08.666
An official letter has no type heading, and each letter should cover only one topic.

38
00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:11.964
Minutes must be drafted on the spot and signed by all parties present.

39
00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:15.341
A report follows a four-part flow: the situation, the results achieved,

40
00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:17.100
the limitations, and the way forward.

41
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.654
For commercial documents: correspondence should meet the five-C standard — clear,

42
00:02:23.654 --> 00:02:25.756
concise, correct, complete and courteous.

43
00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:28.604
A quotation must always state how long it remains valid.

44
00:02:28.604 --> 00:02:30.715
A contract needs all its essential terms,

45
00:02:30.715 --> 00:02:34.626
and a deal is only complete with all three documents in place: the contract,

46
00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:37.200
the acceptance record, and the liquidation record.

47
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.018
Three things to remember.

48
00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:43.400
Proper formality is a document's passport.

49
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.952
Every type of document has its own structure.

50
00:02:45.952 --> 00:02:49.127
And commercial documents protect a company's reputation.

51
00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:53.073
Go ahead and do the forty multiple-choice questions for Chapter Five,

52
00:02:53.073 --> 00:02:56.046
then get ready for the three computer-lab exercises.
